<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferrante II Gonzaga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1563">1563</a>–1630</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Ferrante II Gonzaga, Duke of Guastalla</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferrante II Gonzaga was Count and from 1621 Duke of Guastalla, a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrante-i-gonzaga">Ferrante I Gonzaga</a>. A poet and diplomat in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> service, he obtained from Emperor Ferdinand II the elevation of Guastalla to a duchy. When the main Gonzaga line of Mantua died out in 1627, he claimed its inheritance, a dispute that fed into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-mantuan-succession">War of the Mantuan Succession</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferrante-ii-gonzaga.jpg" alt="Ferrante II Gonzaga" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portr%C3%A4t_von_Ferrante_Gonzaga.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
